# Review: StackPlugin

The spec is out of date with the code. The core works: an article surface for `Collection`
renders each object as a section in a Mosaic stack, sections show the object's icon and label,
collapse is local component state, and the toolbar's Add Section opens `SpaceOperation.OpenObjectForm`.
The code has also grown things the spec does not describe: drag-and-drop reorder, Move up / Move down,
and Collapse all / Expand all.

Much of the spec is not built. There is no `StackViewType` and no per-section view metadata: the
plugin registers a placeholder `Stack` type (`org.dxos.type.stack`, empty struct, marked
`TODO(burdon): Placeholder`). `StackSectionView`, `StackSectionMetadata`, `AddSectionPosition` and
the settings panel do not exist; only translation strings for separation and navigate remain. The
section menu has no Navigate and no Add Before. Remove splices the ref out of the collection
directly instead of invoking `SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects`. No test exercises the plugin: the e2e
suite only toggles it on and off, and the story has no play function.

